            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Using 365 days per year, convert the duration to seconds and multiply by the speed of light.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Assume a year has 365 days. Let $t$ be the number of seconds in one year and $d$ the distance across the galaxy.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}t&=365\\times24\\times60\\times60\\text{ s}\\\\t&=3.1536\\times10^7\\text{ s}\\\\d&=(8\\times10^4)(3.1536\\times10^7)(3\\times10^5)\\text{ km}\\\\d&=7.56864\\times10^{17}\\text{ km}\\\\d&\\approx7.57\\times10^{17}\\text{ km}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
